# Product Context

**Trigger**: Always active. Load these docs before any feature implementation or UI design work.

## Canonical Product Docs

| Doc | Path | When to Read |
|-----|------|--------------|
| Design Intent | `DESIGN.md` | Before any UI component work — page blueprints, interaction patterns, design decisions |
| MVP Scope | `docs/mvp-scope.md` | Before adding features — confirms what is in/out of scope for v1 |
| Product Vision | `docs/tool-vision-and-market-research.md` | Before planning new features — understand AI-native positioning, target users, monetization |
| User Flows | `docs/user-flows-ai-native.md` | Before implementing screen interactions — step-by-step user journeys | Before implementing AI features — agent patterns, brand voice, credit system |

## Usage Rules

1. **DESIGN.md** → Follow existing page blueprints when they match your feature. For new pages, propose changes consistent with the established design language.

2. **mvp-scope.md** → Do not implement features marked "out of scope" for MVP. If uncertain, check the explicit out-of-scope section first.

3. **tool-vision-and-market-research.md** → Align feature proposals with the AI-native vision (AI as default, not optional add-on) and credit-based monetization model.

4. **user-flows-ai-native.md** → Match existing user flow patterns before inventing new interaction models.

## Priority Order

MVP scope > Design system > User flows > Vision. Scope boundaries are the hard constraint; everything else is guidance.
